# Canonical Context Preflight v1

Before giving progress, routing, next-action, client-delivery, merge, deployment, environment-classification, or blocker advice — and before starting implementation — refresh the current canonical context from GitHub/repo state.

## Mandatory reads

1. `docs/operations/CORPFLOWAI_CURRENT_DELIVERY_REALITY.md`
2. `docs/operations/CORPFLOW_ENVIRONMENT_CLASSIFICATION_V1.md`
3. The current source issue / PR being acted on.

Read additional topic-specific doctrine only when the packet touches that topic.

## Mandatory internal resolution

Resolve all four before proceeding:

- `operating_model_version`: current version from `CORPFLOWAI_CURRENT_DELIVERY_REALITY.md`
- `environment`: one of `corpflow_test`, `client_production`, `local`, `n/a`
- `github_state_refreshed`: `YES`
- `source_item`: current issue/PR number or `n/a`

Do not answer or implement from remembered orchestration assumptions when current GitHub/repo state can be checked.

## Environment rule

CorpFlowAI-controlled tenant/factory hosts under CorpFlowAI infrastructure are `corpflow_test` unless a separate client-production transition is explicitly approved.

A Vercel Preview is optional internal verification only. Do not require a preview environment before publishing a normal tenant change to `corpflow_test`.

`client_production` means a separately governed client-owned/client-approved external production target. It is never inferred merely because Vercel calls the serving spine “Production”.

## PR acknowledgement

New agent-authored PRs created after Canonical Context Preflight v1 activation must include this block in the PR body:

```text
Canonical Context Preflight: PASS
Operating model version: <current version>
Environment: corpflow_test | client_production | local | n/a
GitHub state refreshed: YES
Source item: #<issue> | PR #<number> | n/a
```

The repository CI gate validates this acknowledgement for new PRs. This acknowledgement is evidence of refresh, not authorization for any protected action.

The `Environment:` acknowledgement must be a bare enum on its own line. Do not append notes on that line (`Environment: n/a (control plane only)` fails if no later bare `Environment: n/a` exists). The checker accepts the first exact allowed enum in the PR body, so a later acknowledgement block still wins over an earlier narrative `Environment:` line with extra text.

## Protected actions unchanged

This rule does not authorize merge, client-production deploy, env/secrets changes, DB/schema changes, payments, external sends/outreach, paid tools, or public client launch. Existing durable-approval gates remain authoritative.
